# Copy to .devcontainer/devcontainer.env (GITIGNORED — see the repo's .gitignore) and fill in.
#
# Passed to `docker run` via the "runArgs": ["--env-file", ...] in devcontainer.json, so it
# is picked up automatically at container start. Nothing needs to be exported in the shell
# that launched VS Code, and none of it is baked into an image layer.

# Your Forgejo API token. Unlike the signing key in the signed-commits example, this IS a
# secret — treat it like a password.
#
# Create it on your instance under Settings -> Applications -> Access Tokens. Scopes:
#   read:user         (required — the CLI identifies you with it)
#   write:issue       to file and comment on issues
#   write:repository  additionally, to open pull requests
#
# The container re-reads this on every attach, so rotating the token is just: edit this
# file, then reconnect. No rebuild needed.
FORGEJO_TOKEN=
